@lang en
IMPORT `vn11-death-claim`

-- Manulife Vietnam term life product terms, row VN-11: tests. Every expected value was worked by
-- hand from the source text (the lines are cited) before the assertion was written, by the same
-- session that wrote the rules; no independent test pass has been run (NOTES.md section 6). The
-- document prints no worked example. The Art 3(b) rows are generated from the raw text by a script
-- (vn11_table3b.py, run at build time and not deposited) rather than retyped.
-- Records whose fields share a type are built WITH named fields; positional OF is used only where
-- every field has a type of its own (`A death claim`, `A premium instalment`, `A dispute`,
-- `A beneficiary designation`, `A termination under Art 18`), so no two fields can trade places.

§ `Fixtures`

§§ `The contract page`

-- A sum insured of 1 billion dong; effective 15 January 2020, issued 1 February 2020 (later, as a
-- contract usually is), maturing 15 January 2040.
`the standard contract page` MEANS
    `The contract page` WITH
        `sum insured`    IS 1_000_000_000
        `effective date` IS YMD 2020 1 15
        `maturity date`  IS YMD 2040 1 15
        `issue date`     IS YMD 2020 2 1

-- A child's contract: effective 5 January 2022, issued 10 January 2022, maturing 5 January 2042.
`the child's contract page` MEANS
    `The contract page` WITH
        `sum insured`    IS 1_000_000_000
        `effective date` IS YMD 2022 1 5
        `maturity date`  IS YMD 2042 1 5
        `issue date`     IS YMD 2022 1 10

§§ `The application`

`a signed application` MEANS
    `The application` WITH
        `signed by the policyholder`               IS TRUE
        `signed by the insured`                    IS TRUE
        `Age misstated in it`                      IS FALSE
        `sex misstated in it`                      IS FALSE
        `address of the policyholder stated in it` IS "12 Le Loi Street, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City"

`an application the insured did not sign` MEANS
    `The application` WITH
        `signed by the policyholder`               IS TRUE
        `signed by the insured`                    IS FALSE
        `Age misstated in it`                      IS FALSE
        `sex misstated in it`                      IS FALSE
        `address of the policyholder stated in it` IS "12 Le Loi Street, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City"

`an application with the Age misstated` MEANS
    `The application` WITH
        `signed by the policyholder`               IS TRUE
        `signed by the insured`                    IS TRUE
        `Age misstated in it`                      IS TRUE
        `sex misstated in it`                      IS FALSE
        `address of the policyholder stated in it` IS "12 Le Loi Street, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City"

`an application with the sex misstated` MEANS
    `The application` WITH
        `signed by the policyholder`               IS TRUE
        `signed by the insured`                    IS TRUE
        `Age misstated in it`                      IS FALSE
        `sex misstated in it`                      IS TRUE
        `address of the policyholder stated in it` IS "12 Le Loi Street, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City"

§§ `The insured`

GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The insured`
`a resident insured born on` `the date of birth` MEANS
    `The insured` WITH
        `true date of birth`                   IS `the date of birth`
        `resided in Vietnam on the issue date` IS TRUE
        `also the policyholder`                IS FALSE

GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The insured`
`an insured not resident on the issue date, born on` `the date of birth` MEANS
    `The insured` WITH
        `true date of birth`                   IS `the date of birth`
        `resided in Vietnam on the issue date` IS FALSE
        `also the policyholder`                IS FALSE

-- Born 10 June 1985: Age 34 on 1 February 2020.
`an adult insured, resident in Vietnam` MEANS `a resident insured born on` (YMD 1985 6 10)

§§ `Premiums`

-- 20 million dong of premium paid, all on time; the Company deducts 1 million in costs.
`premiums paid up` MEANS
    `The premium record` WITH
        `first premium paid`                                    IS TRUE
        `instalment in default`                                 IS NOTHING
        `premiums due and unpaid at the death`                  IS 0
        `premiums of the policy year not yet due at the death`  IS 0
        `total premium paid`                                    IS 20_000_000
        `total premium payable at the true Age and sex`         IS 20_000_000
        `reasonable costs and expenses deducted by the Company` IS 1_000_000
        `date of the most recent reinstatement`                 IS NOTHING

`premiums paid up, reinstated on 1 June 2023` MEANS
    `The premium record` WITH
        `first premium paid`                                    IS TRUE
        `instalment in default`                                 IS NOTHING
        `premiums due and unpaid at the death`                  IS 0
        `premiums of the policy year not yet due at the death`  IS 0
        `total premium paid`                                    IS 20_000_000
        `total premium payable at the true Age and sex`         IS 20_000_000
        `reasonable costs and expenses deducted by the Company` IS 1_000_000
        `date of the most recent reinstatement`                 IS JUST (YMD 2023 6 1)

-- 9 million paid where 12 million was payable at the true Age and sex.
`premiums of 9 million where 12 million was payable` MEANS
    `The premium record` WITH
        `first premium paid`                                    IS TRUE
        `instalment in default`                                 IS NOTHING
        `premiums due and unpaid at the death`                  IS 0
        `premiums of the policy year not yet due at the death`  IS 0
        `total premium paid`                                    IS 9_000_000
        `total premium payable at the true Age and sex`         IS 12_000_000
        `reasonable costs and expenses deducted by the Company` IS 1_000_000
        `date of the most recent reinstatement`                 IS NOTHING

`no premium paid` MEANS
    `The premium record` WITH
        `first premium paid`                                    IS FALSE
        `instalment in default`                                 IS NOTHING
        `premiums due and unpaid at the death`                  IS 0
        `premiums of the policy year not yet due at the death`  IS 0
        `total premium paid`                                    IS 0
        `total premium payable at the true Age and sex`         IS 0
        `reasonable costs and expenses deducted by the Company` IS 0
        `date of the most recent reinstatement`                 IS NOTHING

-- An instalment due 15 January 2023. Its grace period runs to 16 March 2023: 16 days to the end
-- of January, 28 in February, 16 in March, 60 in all (src:155-156).
GIVEN `the payment` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the payee`   IS A `A payee of the premium`
GIVETH A `A premium instalment`
`the instalment due 15 January 2023, paid` `the payment` `to` `the payee` MEANS
    `A premium instalment` OF YMD 2023 1 15, `the payment`, `the payee`

GIVEN `the instalment` IS A `A premium instalment`
      `the unpaid`     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The premium record`
`premiums with` `the instalment` `in default and` `the unpaid` `unpaid at the death` MEANS
    `The premium record` WITH
        `first premium paid`                                    IS TRUE
        `instalment in default`                                 IS JUST `the instalment`
        `premiums due and unpaid at the death`                  IS `the unpaid`
        `premiums of the policy year not yet due at the death`  IS 0
        `total premium paid`                                    IS 20_000_000
        `total premium payable at the true Age and sex`         IS 20_000_000
        `reasonable costs and expenses deducted by the Company` IS 1_000_000
        `date of the most recent reinstatement`                 IS NOTHING

`the instalment of 15 January 2023, never paid` MEANS
    `the instalment due 15 January 2023, paid` NOTHING `to` `paid to the Company`

§§ `Disclosure`

`nothing undisclosed` MEANS
    `The disclosure record` WITH
        `material information not disclosed or misstated`           IS FALSE
        `the omission not itself declared by the person concerned`  IS FALSE
        `fraud`                                                     IS FALSE
        `the Company has treated the contract as void under Art 10` IS FALSE

`a misstatement the Company has acted on` MEANS
    `The disclosure record` WITH
        `material information not disclosed or misstated`           IS TRUE
        `the omission not itself declared by the person concerned`  IS TRUE
        `fraud`                                                     IS FALSE
        `the Company has treated the contract as void under Art 10` IS TRUE

`a fraudulent misstatement the Company has acted on` MEANS
    `The disclosure record` WITH
        `material information not disclosed or misstated`           IS TRUE
        `the omission not itself declared by the person concerned`  IS TRUE
        `fraud`                                                     IS TRUE
        `the Company has treated the contract as void under Art 10` IS TRUE

`a misstatement the Company has not acted on` MEANS
    `The disclosure record` WITH
        `material information not disclosed or misstated`           IS TRUE
        `the omission not itself declared by the person concerned`  IS TRUE
        `fraud`                                                     IS FALSE
        `the Company has treated the contract as void under Art 10` IS FALSE

`a misstatement since declared, acted on` MEANS
    `The disclosure record` WITH
        `material information not disclosed or misstated`           IS TRUE
        `the omission not itself declared by the person concerned`  IS FALSE
        `fraud`                                                     IS FALSE
        `the Company has treated the contract as void under Art 10` IS TRUE

§§ `The policyholder's requests`

`no requests` MEANS
    `The policyholder's requests` WITH
        `date the contract was received`              IS YMD 2020 2 5
        `date a written request to cancel was sent`   IS NOTHING
        `date the policyholder requested termination` IS NOTHING

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The policyholder's requests`
`a request to cancel sent on` `the day` MEANS
    `The policyholder's requests` WITH
        `date the contract was received`              IS YMD 2020 2 5
        `date a written request to cancel was sent`   IS JUST `the day`
        `date the policyholder requested termination` IS NOTHING

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The policyholder's requests`
`a request to terminate made on` `the day` MEANS
    `The policyholder's requests` WITH
        `date the contract was received`              IS YMD 2020 2 5
        `date a written request to cancel was sent`   IS NOTHING
        `date the policyholder requested termination` IS JUST `the day`

§§ `The death`

GIVEN `the day`     IS A DATE
      `suicide`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `own crime`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `other crime` IS A BOOLEAN
      `HIV`         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The death`
`a death` `the day` `suicide` `own crime` `other crime` `HIV` MEANS
    `The death` WITH
        `date of death` IS `the day`
        `by suicide`    IS `suicide`
        `resulting directly or indirectly from the insured committing a crime, or intentionally committing a criminal offence` IS `own crime`
        `resulting directly or indirectly from a crime committed by someone other than the insured`                           IS `other crime`
        `related to AIDS, an AIDS-related condition (ARC), or HIV infection`                                                 IS `HIV`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The death`
`a natural death on` `the day` MEANS `a death` `the day` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The death`
`a suicide on` `the day` MEANS `a death` `the day` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The death`
`a death from the insured's own crime on` `the day` MEANS `a death` `the day` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The death`
`a death from another person's crime on` `the day` MEANS `a death` `the day` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The death`
`a death related to HIV on` `the day` MEANS `a death` `the day` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

§§ `The claim`

GIVEN `the day`         IS A DATE
      `the contract`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Age`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `earlier proof`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `force majeure`   IS A NUMBER
      `learned`         IS A MAYBE DATE
      `riders`          IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The claim`
`a claim` `the day` `the contract` `the Age` `earlier proof` `force majeure` `learned` `riders` MEANS
    `The claim` WITH
        `date the claim was made`                            IS `the day`
        `proof of death received`                            IS TRUE
        `the contract provided`                              IS `the contract`
        `the Company's forms completed`                      IS TRUE
        `evidence of the claimants' relationship provided`   IS TRUE
        `evidence of the insured event provided`             IS TRUE
        `evidence of the insured's Age provided`             IS `the Age`
        `proof of age submitted earlier`                     IS `earlier proof`
        `days of force majeure or other objective obstacle`  IS `force majeure`
        `date the policyholder learned of the insured event` IS `learned`
        `rider benefits payable`                             IS `riders`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The claim`
`a complete claim made on` `the day` MEANS `a claim` `the day` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 NOTHING 0

GIVEN `the riders` IS A NUMBER
      `the day`    IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The claim`
`a complete claim with rider benefits of` `the riders` `, made on` `the day` MEANS `a claim` `the day` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 NOTHING `the riders`

§§ `Cases`

-- The standard case, varying the death; the claim is made 30 days after it.
GIVEN `the death` IS A `The death`
GIVETH A `A death claim`
`the standard case with` `the death` MEANS
    `A death claim` OF `the standard contract page`, `a signed application`, `an adult insured, resident in Vietnam`,
                       `premiums paid up`, `nothing undisclosed`, `no requests`, `the death`,
                       `a complete claim made on` (`the death`'s `date of death` PLUS 30)

GIVEN `the premiums` IS A `The premium record`
      `the death`    IS A `The death`
GIVETH A `A death claim`
`the standard case with premiums` `the premiums` `and the death` `the death` MEANS
    `A death claim` OF `the standard contract page`, `a signed application`, `an adult insured, resident in Vietnam`,
                       `the premiums`, `nothing undisclosed`, `no requests`, `the death`,
                       `a complete claim made on` (`the death`'s `date of death` PLUS 30)

GIVEN `the requests` IS A `The policyholder's requests`
      `the death`    IS A `The death`
GIVETH A `A death claim`
`the standard case with requests` `the requests` `and the death` `the death` MEANS
    `A death claim` OF `the standard contract page`, `a signed application`, `an adult insured, resident in Vietnam`,
                       `premiums paid up`, `nothing undisclosed`, `the requests`, `the death`,
                       `a complete claim made on` (`the death`'s `date of death` PLUS 30)

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A `The disclosure record`
      `the death`      IS A `The death`
GIVETH A `A death claim`
`the standard case with disclosure` `the disclosure` `and the death` `the death` MEANS
    `A death claim` OF `the standard contract page`, `a signed application`, `an adult insured, resident in Vietnam`,
                       `premiums paid up`, `the disclosure`, `no requests`, `the death`,
                       `a complete claim made on` (`the death`'s `date of death` PLUS 30)

GIVEN `the form`    IS A `The application`
      `the insured` IS A `The insured`
      `the premiums` IS A `The premium record`
GIVETH A `A death claim`
`a case with application` `the form` `insured` `the insured` `and premiums` `the premiums` MEANS
    `A death claim` OF `the standard contract page`, `the form`, `the insured`,
                       `the premiums`, `nothing undisclosed`, `no requests`, `a natural death on` (YMD 2023 5 10),
                       `a complete claim made on` (YMD 2023 6 9)

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A `A death claim`
`a natural death on 10 May 2023, with the claim` `the claim` MEANS
    `A death claim` OF `the standard contract page`, `a signed application`, `an adult insured, resident in Vietnam`,
                       `premiums paid up`, `nothing undisclosed`, `no requests`, `a natural death on` (YMD 2023 5 10),
                       `the claim`

§ `Article 1 — Definitions`

§§ `Art 1.3 — the insurable Ages, both ends (src:29-31)`
#ASSERT `Art 1.3 — an Age from 0 to 60` 0
#ASSERT `Art 1.3 — an Age from 0 to 60` 60
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1.3 — an Age from 0 to 60` 61
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1.3 — an Age from 0 to 60` (0 MINUS 1)

§§ `Art 1.4 — Age at the last birthday (src:32-33)`
-- Born 1 March 2021: Age 0 on 28 February 2022, Age 1 on 1 March 2022.
#ASSERT `the Age of` (`a resident insured born on` (YMD 2021 3 1)) `on` (YMD 2022 2 28) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the Age of` (`a resident insured born on` (YMD 2021 3 1)) `on` (YMD 2022 3 1) EQUALS 1
-- Born 10 June 1985: Age 34 on the issue date, 1 February 2020.
#ASSERT `the Age of` `an adult insured, resident in Vietnam` `on` (YMD 2020 2 1) EQUALS 34

§§ `Art 1.3 in a claim — Age 60 at issue is insurable; Age 61, not misstated, is not answered`
-- Born 10 June 1959: Age 60 on 1 February 2020. A natural death on 10 May 2023 pays the sum insured.
#ASSERT `the outcome of the death claim` (`a case with application` `a signed application` `insured` (`a resident insured born on` (YMD 1959 6 10)) `and premiums` `premiums paid up`) EQUALS `the death benefit is payable` 1_000_000_000
-- Born 10 June 1958: Age 61 at issue, nothing misstated: the document does not say what follows.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the outcome of the death claim` (`a case with application` `a signed application` `insured` (`a resident insured born on` (YMD 1958 6 10)) `and premiums` `premiums paid up`) BECAUSE "Art 1.3 does not say what follows when the contract was issued at an Age outside 0 to 60 that was not misstated"

§§ `Art 1.5 — a valid application needs both signatures (src:43-45)`
#ASSERT `Art 1.5 — the application is valid` `a signed application`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1.5 — the application is valid` `an application the insured did not sign`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the outcome of the death claim` (`a case with application` `an application the insured did not sign` `insured` `an adult insured, resident in Vietnam` `and premiums` `premiums paid up`) BECAUSE "Art 1.5 does not say what follows when the application was not signed by both the policyholder and the insured"

§§ `Art 1.6 — the contract term, both ends (src:54-56)`
-- Death on the effective date: in force. The day before: not.
#ASSERT `the outcome of the death claim` (`the standard case with` (`a natural death on` (YMD 2020 1 15))) EQUALS `the death benefit is payable` 1_000_000_000
#ASSERT `the outcome of the death claim` (`the standard case with` (`a natural death on` (YMD 2020 1 14))) EQUALS `no death benefit: the contract was not in force` "Art 1.6: the death fell outside the contract term"
-- Death on the maturity date: in force (fork F5). The day after: not.
#ASSERT `the outcome of the death claim` (`the standard case with` (`a natural death on` (YMD 2040 1 15))) EQUALS `the death benefit is payable` 1_000_000_000
#ASSERT `the outcome of the death claim` (`the standard case with` (`a natural death on` (YMD 2040 1 16))) EQUALS `no death benefit: the contract was not in force` "Art 1.6: the death fell outside the contract term"

§ `Article 2 — amendments are signed by the General Director or a Deputy (src:70-74)`
`an amendment signed by a Deputy General Director` MEANS
    `An amendment` WITH `in writing` IS TRUE, `signed for the Company by` IS `a Deputy General Director`, `consented to by the policyholder` IS TRUE
`an amendment signed by another officer` MEANS
    `An amendment` WITH `in writing` IS TRUE, `signed for the Company by` IS `another officer`, `consented to by the policyholder` IS TRUE
`an amendment without the policyholder's consent` MEANS
    `An amendment` WITH `in writing` IS TRUE, `signed for the Company by` IS `the General Director`, `consented to by the policyholder` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 2 — the amendment is validly made` `an amendment signed by a Deputy General Director`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2 — the amendment is validly made` `an amendment signed by another officer`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2 — the amendment is validly made` `an amendment without the policyholder's consent`

§ `Article 3 — Benefits`

§§ `Art 3(a) and 3(b) — one block per row of the table (generated from src:101-126)`
-- generated from the row at src:108 and src:110: Ages 0, 20%
#ASSERT `Art 3(b) — the percentage of the sum insured for an Age at death of` 0 EQUALS 20%
#ASSERT `Art 3(a) — the death benefit` 1_000_000_000 0 0 0 EQUALS 200_000_000
-- generated from the row at src:112 and src:114: Ages 1, 40%
#ASSERT `Art 3(b) — the percentage of the sum insured for an Age at death of` 1 EQUALS 40%
#ASSERT `Art 3(a) — the death benefit` 1_000_000_000 1 0 0 EQUALS 400_000_000
-- generated from the row at src:116 and src:118: Ages 2, 60%
#ASSERT `Art 3(b) — the percentage of the sum insured for an Age at death of` 2 EQUALS 60%
#ASSERT `Art 3(a) — the death benefit` 1_000_000_000 2 0 0 EQUALS 600_000_000
-- generated from the row at src:120 and src:122: Ages 3, 80%
#ASSERT `Art 3(b) — the percentage of the sum insured for an Age at death of` 3 EQUALS 80%
#ASSERT `Art 3(a) — the death benefit` 1_000_000_000 3 0 0 EQUALS 800_000_000
-- generated from the row at src:124 and src:126: Ages 4, 60, 100%
#ASSERT `Art 3(b) — the percentage of the sum insured for an Age at death of` 4 EQUALS 100%
#ASSERT `Art 3(a) — the death benefit` 1_000_000_000 4 0 0 EQUALS 1_000_000_000
#ASSERT `Art 3(b) — the percentage of the sum insured for an Age at death of` 60 EQUALS 100%
#ASSERT `Art 3(a) — the death benefit` 1_000_000_000 60 0 0 EQUALS 1_000_000_000

§§ `Art 3(a) — (i) plus (ii) less (iii) (src:83-93)`
-- 1 billion at 100%, plus 50 million of rider benefits, less 5 million unpaid: 1.045 billion.
#ASSERT `Art 3(a) — the death benefit` 1_000_000_000 40 50_000_000 5_000_000 EQUALS 1_045_000_000
-- Art 3(b) reduces (i) only: Age 2, 60% of 1 billion, plus 50 million, less 5 million.
#ASSERT `Art 3(a) — the death benefit` 1_000_000_000 2 50_000_000 5_000_000 EQUALS 645_000_000

§§ `Art 3(c)(i) — the insured's own crime (src:135-137): triggers, and a near miss`
-- Death on 10 May 2023, past the two years of Arts 10 and 11. Refund: 20 million paid, less 1
-- million of costs (src:171-173).
#ASSERT `the outcome of the death claim` (`the standard case with` (`a death from the insured's own crime on` (YMD 2023 5 10))) EQUALS `no death benefit, and the premium is refunded` "Art 3(c)" 19_000_000
-- Near miss: the insured is the victim of someone else's crime. Payable on the reading taken (F6).
#ASSERT `the outcome of the death claim` (`the standard case with` (`a death from another person's crime on` (YMD 2023 5 10))) EQUALS `the death benefit is payable` 1_000_000_000

§§ `Art 3(c)(ii) — AIDS, ARC or HIV (src:139-145): triggers, and a near miss`
#ASSERT `the outcome of the death claim` (`the standard case with` (`a death related to HIV on` (YMD 2023 5 10))) EQUALS `no death benefit, and the premium is refunded` "Art 3(c)" 19_000_000
#ASSERT `the outcome of the death claim` (`the standard case with` (`a natural death on` (YMD 2023 5 10))) EQUALS `the death benefit is payable` 1_000_000_000

§§ `Art 3(c), last sentence — the refund is the premium less the costs, never below nil`
#ASSERT `the premium refunded, without interest, after the reasonable costs` 20_000_000 1_000_000 EQUALS 19_000_000
#ASSERT `the premium refunded, without interest, after the reasonable costs` 1_000_000 3_000_000 EQUALS 0

§ `Article 4 — the 14 days (src:185-195)`

-- Received 5 February 2020. Sent on 19 February, the 14th day after: in time. 20 February: late.
-- Refund: 5 million paid less 1.5 million of medical expenses.
GIVEN `the day sent` IS A DATE
      `returned`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A request to cancel under Art 4`
`a request to cancel a contract received on 5 February 2020, sent on` `the day sent` `, receipts returned` `returned` MEANS
    `A request to cancel under Art 4` WITH
        `date the contract was received`                          IS YMD 2020 2 5
        `date the written request was sent`                       IS `the day sent`
        `premium paid`                                            IS 5_000_000
        `medical expenses the Company paid in assessing the risk` IS 1_500_000
        `premium receipts returned to the Company`                IS `returned`

#ASSERT `Art 4 — the result of the request to cancel` (`a request to cancel a contract received on 5 February 2020, sent on` (YMD 2020 2 19) `, receipts returned` TRUE) EQUALS `cancelled, and the premium is refunded` 3_500_000
#ASSERT `Art 4 — the result of the request to cancel` (`a request to cancel a contract received on 5 February 2020, sent on` (YMD 2020 2 20) `, receipts returned` TRUE) EQUALS `not cancelled under Art 4: the request was late`
-- The receipts not returned: nothing is refunded (src:192-195).
#ASSERT `Art 4 — the result of the request to cancel` (`a request to cancel a contract received on 5 February 2020, sent on` (YMD 2020 2 19) `, receipts returned` FALSE) EQUALS `cancelled, and nothing is refunded`

-- In a claim: cancelled on 10 February, death on 1 March: not in force. A late request (25
-- February) does not cancel, and the death benefit is payable.
#ASSERT `the outcome of the death claim` (`the standard case with requests` (`a request to cancel sent on` (YMD 2020 2 10)) `and the death` (`a natural death on` (YMD 2020 3 1))) EQUALS `no death benefit: the contract was not in force` "Art 4: the policyholder had cancelled the contract"
#ASSERT `the outcome of the death claim` (`the standard case with requests` (`a request to cancel sent on` (YMD 2020 2 25)) `and the death` (`a natural death on` (YMD 2020 3 1))) EQUALS `the death benefit is payable` 1_000_000_000

-- The permission, in days from receipt: sent on day 14, receipts returned, refund paid.
#TRACE `Art 4 — the policyholder may cancel within 14 days of receiving the contract` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the policyholder` DOES `send the Company a written request to cancel` AT 14
    PARTY `the policyholder` DOES `return the premium receipts to the Company` AT 20
    PARTY `the Company` DOES `refund the premium paid, less the medical expenses of assessing the risk` AT 30

§ `Article 5 — premiums and the grace period (src:147-179)`

§§ `Art 5 — deemed not paid, and the last day of grace`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5 — the instalment is deemed not paid` (`the instalment due 15 January 2023, paid` (JUST (YMD 2023 1 15)) `to` `paid to the Company`)
#ASSERT `Art 5 — the instalment is deemed not paid` (`the instalment due 15 January 2023, paid` (JUST (YMD 2023 1 16)) `to` `paid to the Company`)
#ASSERT `Art 5 — the last day of the grace period for` `the instalment of 15 January 2023, never paid` EQUALS YMD 2023 3 16

§§ `Art 5 — a death in the grace period, and the day after it`
-- Death on 16 March 2023, the last day of grace, 5 million unpaid: 1 billion less 5 million.
